//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: no rule for marker `Ord`

// A marker is satisfied by a rule the compiler owns, so which marker a bound names has to be
// settled by IDENTITY rather than by spelling.
//
// `is_known_marker` matched the bare name, so `marker Ord` declared in any module was
// accepted -- while `marker Frobnicable` next to it is correctly rejected as having no rule.
// The user's marker then silently meant whatever the prelude's `Ord` means, in a module that
// never asked for it, and `satisfies_marker` answered it from the built-in structural rule.
//
// This is `docs/design/identity.md`'s lesson one declaration kind over, and it is the same
// shape as the bare-name matches that produced the impl-body and derive collisions: a key
// that two different declarations can produce.
//
// Recorded as unproven lead L1 and confirmed 2026-08-04. The prelude has a reserved module
// path of its own (`Env::PRELUDE`) that no source can write, which is exactly what makes the
// identity test possible.

use std::io;

internal mod mine {
    marker Ord
}

fn main() {
    io::println("this must not compile");
}
